{
  "slug": "geometric-series-oq-02",
  "title": "Geometric Series for Matrices and Operators",
  "phase": "COMPLETED",
  "status": "graduated",
  "tier": "A",
  "path": "fast",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "In a complete normed ring, prove that if ||T|| < 1 then the Neumann series sum_n T^n is summable, 1 - T is a unit, and the infinite sum equals Ring.inverse (1 - T), with finite-sum identities, inverse identities, norm bounds, and perturbation corollaries.",
    "plain": "Extend the scalar geometric series to operators and complete normed rings: a small element T has a convergent Neumann series, and that series is the inverse of 1 - T.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Neumann series are the standard bridge from geometric series to operator inverses and perturbation theory.",
      "The proof packages invertibility, partial sums, and norm bounds in a reusable algebraic-analysis form.",
      "The same pattern underlies resolvent identities and local invertibility results for normed algebras."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "For ||T|| < 1 in a complete normed ring, the power series n |-> T^n is summable (Lean: neumann_summable).",
      "The element 1 - T is a unit and the Neumann sum equals Ring.inverse (1 - T) (Lean: one_sub_isUnit, neumann_sum).",
      "Finite left and right geometric identities are proved for ring elements (Lean: finite_neumann_identity, finite_neumann_identity').",
      "The infinite Neumann sum is both a left and right inverse of 1 - T, and satisfies a norm bound (Lean: left_inverse_identity, right_inverse_identity, norm_neumann_le).",
      "Partial sums converge to the inverse, and nearby elements with ||1 - A|| < 1 are invertible (Lean: partial_sums_tendsto, invertible_near_one, inverse_near_one)."
    ],
    "open": [],
    "goal": "Record the verified complete-normed-ring Neumann-series theorem and its operator-style consequences."
  },
